SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Kyriaki\, Koumaradaioi
LOCATION:Koumaradaioi\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:At the chapel of Agia Kyriaki on the edge of Koumaradaioi\, on the road to Pyrgos\, the village's church-and-volunteer-firefighters association stages a feast on the evening of 6 July with an island-music orchestra in the church courtyard and the road outside\, souvlaki\, paspalas (the local pork-and-egg dish)\, pancakes and salads\; liturgy and refreshments follow on the morning of the 7th. A classic inland Samos panigiri\, 20 minutes from Pythagoreio.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#koumaradaioi-panigiri-of-agia-kyriaki-koumaradaioi
